1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,829
Rent is collected in a handful of cheques
but

2
00:00:03,829 --> 00:00:07,658
earned every day, so this tutorial closes
a month.

3
00:00:07,658 --> 00:00:12,338
Start on a posted contract and open its
Recognition schedule tab.

4
00:00:12,338 --> 00:00:16,592
RentAxis divided the term by its actual
number of days

5
00:00:16,592 --> 00:00:20,847
to get a daily rate, then multiplied that
rate by

6
00:00:20,847 --> 00:00:24,676
the real number of days in each calendar
month.

7
00:00:24,676 --> 00:00:29,781
A twelve month contract that starts mid
month therefore opens with a

8
00:00:29,781 --> 00:00:34,461
short period and closes with another, and
the last row absorbs

9
00:00:34,461 --> 00:00:39,140
any rounding so the schedule adds up to
the rent exactly.

10
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:42,119
Every row shows its period, its day

11
00:00:42,119 --> 00:00:44,671
count, its amount and its status.

12
00:00:44,671 --> 00:00:47,649
Rows are planned until they are posted.

13
00:00:47,649 --> 00:00:50,202
Now open Finance and choose Recognition.

14
00:00:50,202 --> 00:00:54,031
Enter the date you are closing to,
normally the

15
00:00:54,031 --> 00:00:57,434
last day of last month, and select
Preview.

16
00:00:57,434 --> 00:01:01,263
RentAxis lists every planned row across
every contract that

17
00:01:01,263 --> 00:01:05,092
ends on or before that date, with a total.

18
00:01:05,092 --> 00:01:09,347
Read the total before you post it; this is
the

19
00:01:09,347 --> 00:01:13,601
rental income you are about to recognise
for the period.

20
00:01:13,601 --> 00:01:14,452
Select Run.

21
00:01:14,452 --> 00:01:18,706
Each row becomes one journal dated the
last day of

22
00:01:18,706 --> 00:01:22,961
its own period, debiting advance rent and
crediting rental income,

23
00:01:22,961 --> 00:01:26,790
with the narration Advance rent adjustment
and the month.

24
00:01:26,790 --> 00:01:31,044
Dating these entries at the period end
rather than the

25
00:01:31,044 --> 00:01:35,299
first of the next month is deliberate, so
a month's

26
00:01:35,299 --> 00:01:39,128
income falls inside the month it was
earned in.

27
00:01:39,128 --> 00:01:43,807
Open the General Ledger and filter to the
advance rent account.

28
00:01:43,807 --> 00:01:48,062
The balance falls by exactly what you just
recognised, and

29
00:01:48,062 --> 00:01:51,891
the rental income account rises by the
same amount.

30
00:01:51,891 --> 00:01:55,294
Recognition also runs automatically each
night, so a

31
00:01:55,294 --> 00:01:58,272
backdated contract catches up on its own.

32
00:01:58,272 --> 00:02:02,952
Running it by hand is for closing a period
on purpose,

33
00:02:02,952 --> 00:02:07,632
and for the first catch-up after you move
your books across.
